ZVSE2

** WEALTH OF EREBUS - combination artifact made of two combination artifacts (misc slot)
**
** Parts: Minerjack (281) + Cornucopia (140).
** When combined, the parts no longer count as owned, so their resources are replaced by:
**   - +10 Wood, Ore, Mercury, Sulfur, Crystal and Gems and +2 Mithril per day,
**     equipped or in the backpack.
**   - Loot: after defeating a hero of another player, 10% of one random resource of that player
**     (Wood, Ore, Mercury, Sulfur, Crystal, Gems or Gold, only resources the player has at least
**     10 of) is taken from them and given to you. No loot from neutral battles.
** Price: the sum of its parts (Minerjack 10000 + Cornucopia's parts 4 x 5000).
**
** Artifact 282. The game's combination system can't use combination artifacts as parts, so this
** script combines them: when a hero screen is closed with both equipped, the player is asked. Icon: artifact.def frame 282 and Emerald's artraits.txt row 282
** (Data/EmeraldArtifacts.pac and Data/00 forge and fury.pac), png in Data/forge and fury.zip.
** Enabled/disabled in WoG Options -> Custom Scripts, option 955 "Custom Artifacts" (shared by all new artifacts).

; ============= SETTINGS ===========================================================================

!#DC(WOE_OPTION)            = 955;       [shared option "Custom Artifacts"]
!#DC(WOE_ART)               = 282;
!#DC(WOE_MINERJACK)         = 281;
!#DC(WOE_COST)              = 30000;
!#DC(WOE_ART_CLASS)         = 16;       [Relic]
!#DC(WOE_ART_POSITION)      = 9;        [Misc slot (ERM Format P2)]

!#DC(WOE_RES_PER_DAY)       = 10;       [Wood, Ore, Mercury, Sulfur, Crystal, Gems]
!#DC(WOE_MITHRIL_PER_DAY)   = 2;
!#DC(WOE_LOOT_PCT)          = 10;       [% of one enemy resource after defeating an enemy hero]
!#DC(WOE_LOOT_TAKE_FROM_ENEMY) = 1;     [1 = the enemy loses what you get, 0 = you only gain]

!#UN:P(WOE_OPTION)/?i^woe_enabled^;
!#VRi^woe_enabled^|i^cr_hasResound^<>(TRUE):S(FALSE); [needs Resound, see "31 forge and fury - dependencies.erm"]

; Named globals are stored in savegames, so re-read the option after a game is started or loaded
!?FU(OnStartOrLoad);
!!UN:P(WOE_OPTION)/?i^woe_enabled^;
!!VRi^woe_enabled^|i^cr_hasResound^<>(TRUE):S(FALSE); [needs Resound, see "31 forge and fury - dependencies.erm"]

; ============= ARTIFACT SETUP =====================================================================

!?FU(WOE_SetUpArtifact);
!!UN:A(WOE_ART)/1/(WOE_COST);
!!UN:A(WOE_ART)/2/(WOE_ART_POSITION);
!!UN:A(WOE_ART)/3/(WOE_ART_CLASS);
!!UN:A(WOE_ART)/1;                       [never appears on the map: it is only made from its parts]

!!SN:H^art^/(WOE_ART)/0/^Wealth of Erebus^;
!!SN:H^art^/(WOE_ART)/1/^{Wealth of Erebus}

The riches of the underworld, joined from the Minerjack and the Cornucopia. Whoever carries it never lacks anything.

- Every day: +10 Wood, Ore, Mercury, Sulfur, Crystal and Gems and +2 Mithril (equipped or in the backpack).
- After defeating the hero of another player, you seize 10%% of one of that player's resources.^;

; Note: the game's combination system can't use combination artifacts as parts, so the Minerjack and
; the Cornucopia are combined by this script (see COMBINING below), not with UN:A.

!#FU(WOE_SetUpArtifact)&i^woe_enabled^:P;

!?FU(OnAfterLoadGame)&i^woe_enabled^;
!!FU(WOE_SetUpArtifact):P;

; ============= COMBINING ==========================================================================
; When the hero screen is closed and the hero has both the Minerjack and the Cornucopia equipped, ask
; the player whether to combine them. If declined, don't ask again until one of them is re-equipped.
; Computer players combine them automatically (daily check below).

; Returns the equipped slots of both parts, or NO_ART_SLOT
!?FU(WOE_FindParts);
!#VA(hero:x) (slotMinerjack:x) (slotCornucopia:x);

!!VR(slotMinerjack):S(NO_ART_SLOT);
!!VR(slotCornucopia):S(NO_ART_SLOT);

!!re i/(ART_SLOT_EQUIPPED_FIRST)/(ART_SLOT_EQUIPPED_LAST);
  !!FU(GetArtAtSlot):P(hero)/i/?(art:y)/?(artMod:y);
  !!VR(slotMinerjack)&(art)=(WOE_MINERJACK)/(slotMinerjack)=(NO_ART_SLOT):Si;
  !!VR(slotCornucopia)&(art)=(ART_CORNUCOPIA)/(slotCornucopia)=(NO_ART_SLOT):Si;
!!en;

!?FU(WOE_Combine);
!#VA(hero:x) (slotMinerjack:x) (slotCornucopia:x);

!!FU(UnequipArtFromSlot):P(hero)/(slotMinerjack);
!!FU(UnequipArtFromSlot):P(hero)/(slotCornucopia);
!!FU(AddArtToHero):P(hero)/(WOE_ART)/(NO_ART_MOD)/?(ok:y);

; Re-equipping one of the parts allows asking again
!?AE1&i^woe_enabled^;
!!FU&v998<>(WOE_MINERJACK)/v998<>(ART_CORNUCOPIA):E;
!!HE-1:N?(hero:y);
!!VRi^woe_declined_%(hero)^:S(FALSE);

!?FU(OnCloseHeroScreen)&i^woe_enabled^;
!!HE-1:N?(hero:y);
!!FU&(hero)<=(NO_HERO):E;
!!FU&i^woe_declined_%(hero)^:E;

!!FU(WOE_FindParts):P(hero)/?(slotMinerjack:y)/?(slotCornucopia:y);
!!FU|(slotMinerjack)=(NO_ART_SLOT)/(slotCornucopia)=(NO_ART_SLOT):E;

!!HE(hero):O?(owner:y);
!!OW:I(owner)/?(isAi:y);
!!FU&(isAi):E;                           [computer players: see the daily check]

!!IF:Q1/(PIC_TYPE_ART)/(WOE_ART)/(MSG_TYPE_QUESTION)^Combine the Minerjack and the Cornucopia into the {Wealth of Erebus}?^;

!!if&1;
  !!FU(WOE_Combine):P(hero)/(slotMinerjack)/(slotCornucopia);
!!el;
  !!VRi^woe_declined_%(hero)^:S(TRUE);
!!en;

; ============= DAILY RESOURCES ====================================================================
; Once per day (first player of the day), from day 2 on - like the game's own resource artifacts.

!?FU(OnEveryDay)&i^woe_enabled^/i^timerOnce^=1/i^timerDay^>1;
!!re i/(HERO_FIRST)/(HERO_LAST_WOG);
  !!HEi:O?(owner:y);
  !!co&(owner)<=(NO_OWNER);

  ; Computer players combine the parts automatically
  !!OW:I(owner)/?(isAi:y);
  !!if&(isAi);
    !!FU(WOE_FindParts):Pi/?(slotMinerjack:y)/?(slotCornucopia:y);
    !!FU(WOE_Combine)&(slotMinerjack)<>(NO_ART_SLOT)/(slotCornucopia)<>(NO_ART_SLOT):Pi/(slotMinerjack)/(slotCornucopia);
  !!en;

  !!HEi:A2/(WOE_ART)/?(count:y)/?(equipped:y);  [count = equipped + backpack]
  !!co&(count)<=0;

  !!VR(amount:y):S(count) *(WOE_RES_PER_DAY);
  !!re j/(RES_WOOD)/(RES_GEMS);
    !!OW:R(owner)/j/d(amount);
  !!en;

  !!VR(mithril:y):S(count) *(WOE_MITHRIL_PER_DAY);
  !!OW:R(owner)/(RES_MITHRIL)/d(mithril);
!!en;

; ============= LOOT FROM DEFEATED ENEMY HEROES ====================================================

; Remember the heroes' experience before the battle: a hero that gained experience won
!?FU(OnBeforeBattleUniversal)&i^woe_enabled^;
!!re i/(BATTLE_LEFT)/(BATTLE_RIGHT);
  !!VRi^woe_exp_%i^:S-1;
  !!VR(hero:y):Si^battle_hero_%i^;
  !!co&(hero)<=(NO_HERO);
  !!HE(hero):E?i^woe_exp_%i^;
!!en;

!?FU(OnAfterBattleUniversal)&i^woe_enabled^/i^battle_hero_vs_hero^;
!!re i/(BATTLE_LEFT)/(BATTLE_RIGHT);
  !!FU(WOE_TakeLoot):Pi;
!!en;

!?FU(WOE_TakeLoot);
!#VA(side:x);
!#VA(candidates[7]:y);

!!VR(hero:y):Si^battle_hero_%(side)^;
!!FU&(hero)<=(NO_HERO):E;

!!HE(hero):A2/(WOE_ART)/?(count:y)/?(equipped:y);
!!FU&(count)<=0:E;

; Won the battle?
!!HE(hero):E?(expAfter:y);
!!FU&(expAfter)<=i^woe_exp_%(side)^:E;

; The loser must be another player (not neutral, not an ally of the same colour)
!!VR(enemySide:y):S(side) X(TRUE);
!!VR(owner:y):Si^battle_owner_%(side)^;
!!VR(enemy:y):Si^battle_owner_%(enemySide)^;
!!FU|(enemy)<=(NO_OWNER)/(owner)<=(NO_OWNER)/(enemy)=(owner):E;

; Pick a random resource the enemy has at least 10 of (so that 10% is at least 1)
!!VR(numCandidates:y):S0;
!!re j/(RES_WOOD)/(RES_GOLD);
  !!OW:R(enemy)/j/?(have:y);
  !!co&(have)<10;
  !!VR(candidates[numCandidates]):Sj;
  !!VR(numCandidates):+1;
!!en;
!!FU&(numCandidates)<=0:E;

!!VR(lastIndex:y):S(numCandidates) -1;
!!VR(pick:y):R0/0/(lastIndex);         [random 0..numCandidates-1]
!!VR(res:y):S(candidates[pick]);
!!OW:R(enemy)/(res)/?(have);
!!VR(loot:y):S(have) *(WOE_LOOT_PCT) :100;

!!VR(takeFromEnemy:y):S(WOE_LOOT_TAKE_FROM_ENEMY);
!!VR(negLoot:y):S(loot) *-1;
!!OW&(takeFromEnemy)=1:R(enemy)/(res)/d(negLoot);
!!OW:R(owner)/(res)/d(loot);

!!OW:I(owner)/?(isAi:y);
!!IF&(isAi)<>(TRUE):Q1/(res)/(loot)/(MSG_TYPE_MES)^{Wealth of Erebus}

The riches of the defeated flow into your treasury.^;
